      "summaries": {
        "en": "VibeVoice is an open-source voice AI model that enables realistic text-to-speech synthesis, addressing the need for accessible high-quality voice generation without proprietary systems. It leverages advanced neural architectures to produce natural-sounding speech with emotional nuance and diverse vocal characteristics. Developers can integrate it into applications for accessibility tools, content creation, or interactive systems, experimenting with custom voice training or multilingual support through its Python-based framework.",
        "zh": "VibeVoice 是一个开源语音AI模型，专注于实现高质量的文本转语音合成，解决了依赖闭源系统进行逼真语音生成的难题。它采用先进的神经网络架构，能够生成带有情感色彩和多样音色的自然语音，其核心在于平衡模型效率与输出质量。用户可通过Python框架将其集成到无障碍工具、内容创作或交互式应用中，并可尝试自定义语音训练或多语言扩展，为实际场景提供灵活的声音解决方案。",
        "es": "VibeVoice is an open-source voice AI model that enables realistic text-to-speech synthesis, addressing the need for accessible high-quality voice generation without proprietary systems. It leverages advanced neural architectures to produce natural-sounding speech with emotional nuance and diverse vocal characteristics. Developers can integrate it into applications for accessibility tools, content creation, or interactive systems, experimenting with custom voice training or multilingual support through its Python-based framework.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "VibeVoice gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "VibeVoice is an open-source voice AI model that enables realistic text-to-speech synthesis, addressing the need for accessible high-quality voice generation without proprietary systems. It leverages advanced neural architectures to produce natural-sounding speech with emotional nuance and diverse vocal characteristics. Developers can integrate it into applications for accessibility tools, content creation, or interactive systems, experimenting with custom voice training or multilingual support through its Python-based framework.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/microsoft/VibeVoice for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
